    "evidence_text": "The Yakutian Laika (Russian: \u042f\u043a\u0443\u0442\u0441\u043a\u0430\u044f \u043b\u0430\u0439\u043a\u0430 ) is a working dog breed that originated in the Arctic seashore of the Sakha (Yakutia) Republic.\n\nRusso-European Laika\n\nRusso-European Laika (Russko-Evrope\u012dskaya L\u00e1\u012dka) is the name of a breed of hunting dog that originated in the forested region of northern Europe and Russia, one of several breeds developed from landrace Laika dogs of very ancient Spitz type.\n\n The \"Russo-European Laika\" itself dates to a breeding program begun in 1944 by E. I. Shereshevsky of the All-Union Research Institute for the Hunting Industry, in Kalinin (now Tver) Province.\n\nEast Siberian Laika\n\nThe East Siberian Laika (Vostotchno-Sibirskaia Laika) is a Russian breed of dog of spitz type, a hunting dog originating in parts of Siberia east of the Yenisei River.\n\n Bo is a male Portuguese Water Dog.\n\nPortuguese Podengo\n\nThe Portuguese Podengo is an ancient multi-sensory hound (sight and scent) breed of dog from Portugal.",
